From: Mauro Ribeiro <mauro.ribeiro@hardkernel.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: v4l2: enable HEVC in the stateful video decoder

The V4L2 stateful video decoder hard-stubbed HEVC with NOTIMPLEMENTED()
and returned kUnsupportedCodec on the first Decode(), so HEVC streams
failed with PIPELINE_ERROR_DECODE even though the kernel meson-vdec
driver decodes HEVC fine.

HEVC needs no special host-side framing for this stateful decoder (the
Amlogic esparser parses the Annex-B bitstream itself, same as VP9), so
route HEVC through the generic direct-feed path instead of the H.264
reassembler. Verified decoding 4K HEVC Main on ODROID-C4 (S905X3).

Signed-off-by: Mauro Ribeiro <mauro.ribeiro@hardkernel.com>
---
--- a/media/gpu/v4l2/v4l2_stateful_video_decoder.cc
+++ b/media/gpu/v4l2/v4l2_stateful_video_decoder.cc
@@ -510,11 +510,6 @@
       decoder_buffer_and_callbacks_.push(std::move(a));
     }
 
-  } else if (VideoCodecProfileToVideoCodec(config_.profile()) ==
-             VideoCodec::kHEVC) {
-    NOTIMPLEMENTED();
-    std::move(decode_cb).Run(DecoderStatus::Codes::kUnsupportedCodec);
-    return;
   } else {
     decoder_buffer_and_callbacks_.emplace(std::move(buffer),
                                           std::move(decode_cb));
